  "description": "BUQZET crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H48 Eu4 O24 4+,4(Cl1 O4 1-),C2 H6 O1,C1 H4 O1,8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.639-4.095 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.63-115.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu4(μ3-OH)4(μ2-L)4](ClO4)4·C2H6O·CH4O·8H2O (L = 2,6-diformyl-p-cresolate); CCDC C36H48Eu4O24 4+, 4(ClO4−), C2H6O, CH4O, 8(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
